{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"in memory database provider in memory database provider","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md","fileName":"In-Memory Database Provider.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"In-Memory Database Provider","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:37\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Web Application Testing]] [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]] [[ASP.NET Core API Integration Testing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Application Testing","Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core API Integration Testing","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"in memory database provider in memory database provider","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md","fileName":"In-Memory Database Provider.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"In-Memory Database Provider","heading":"In-Memory Database Provider","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An in-memory database provider stores test data in process instead of connecting Entity Framework Core to the production database server. It gives a test a fast, disposable context with known records.\n\nThis supports isolated controller tests without a SQL Server dependency. Because the provider does not reproduce every relational database behavior, it is a unit-testing aid rather than proof that production SQL integration works identically.\n\nThe web-research tests configure a uniquely named EF Core in-memory database through `DbContextOptionsBuilder`. The real context type is then supplied to a controller, allowing create-and-retrieve behavior to be exercised without a persistent SQL Server instance.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Application Testing","Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core API Integration Testing","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"in memory database provider in memory database provider","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/In-Memory Database Provider.md","fileName":"In-Memory Database Provider.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"In-Memory Database Provider","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf]]\n[[hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Web Application Testing","Entity Framework Core Data Access","ASP.NET Core API Integration Testing","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}